    "summary": "(a) The reauth `slots_already_configured` text always sends the user to `{entry_title}` and only covers that entry being disabled. That entry can also be failed (for example, it lost a different lock), and then editing it carries the same leftover-PIN risk the text was written to avoid.",
    "failure_scenario": "Entry Y holds lock L and is itself in SETUP_ERROR because another of its locks is gone. In entry X's reauth the user adds L, gets the refusal, and follows it: 'remove {other_users} from it'. Y has no update listener, so the removed users' codes stay on Y's locks. After both entries recover, those PINs are still on the locks and nothing manages them."
