  {
    "file": "custom_components/lock_code_manager/strings.json",
    "line": 153,
    "summary": "(a) The new base error strings put `{entry_title}` in markdown backticks and nest parentheses (`({users})`, where `users` is already 'Name (n)'). The frontend shows base errors as plain text in `ha-alert` (frontend `ha-form.ts:175-178`), so the backticks appear literally and the parentheses read badly.",
    "failure_scenario": "In the options flow, adding a lock that overlaps the entry 'Home' shows: \"users in this configuration (User 1 (1), User 2 (2)) hold the same slot numbers as users the configuration `Home` already has...\". The backticks and doubled parentheses appear in the dialog as written. This affects both the config and options copies of the string."
  },
  {
    "file": "custom_components/lock_code_manager/config_flow.py",
    "line": 897,
    "summary": "(c) A successful options save on an entry that failed to load does nothing visible. HA's `OptionsFlowManager.async_finish_flow` only writes the options (this is not an `OptionsFlowWithReload`), and the failed entry has no update listener. The new `locks_not_found` refusal implies the opposite: remove the gone lock, save, and it is fixed.",
