toolUseResult.result:
I ran mutations against a scratch copy (now deleted; the worktree was not touched). Everything else checks out:

- **Mutations caught:** the round-1 fixes now hold for #863's code-handler guard, #1623 (both the `desired_credential` owner lookup and the sensor's `owner=` argument), #776 (masked read as unreadable) and #819.
- **Stability:** the full suite passes (2805), and six repeat runs of the e2e and harness files all passed.
- **`LIFELONG_TASKS`:** HA runs `client.listen` inside the listen background task itself, so the registration catches the right task. It is discarded in `finally` and cleared at fixture teardown, so nothing leaks across tests and no Lock Code Manager task is masked.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "tests/providers/zwave_js/test_e2e.py",
    "line": 1325,
    "summary": "The #776 test asserts `writes[slot] <= 1`, so it also passes when a masking lock is never written at all, even though the docstring says each slot is written once and in practice each slot is written exactly once.",
    "failure_scenario": "Mutating `calculate_in_sync`'s unreadable branch from `return snapshot.credential_state == self._last_set_pin` to `return True` (masked slots always count as in sync, so a PIN change or a takeover is never pushed) passes all 41 e2e tests. Changing the assertion to `writes[slot] == 1` still passes on the real code, so the exact count is available and would kill this mutant."
  },
  {
    "file": "tests/providers/zwave_js/test_e2e.py",
    "line": 1128,
    "summary": "The pairings meant to stay unasserted (Available plus \"****\", \"0000\" or \"\" on a slot that wants a PIN) are pinned by three tests already on main, contrary to the 'no test pins them' premise.",
    "failure_scenario": "A mutation that makes the code handler leave a wanted slot alone on Available plus empty, zeros or masked fails `test_a_stale_available_does_not_empty_a_wanted_slot[masked]` (asserts known(\"****\")), `test_events.py::test_uc_shim_zeros_on_available_slot_pushes_empty` (line 732, asserts empty for \"0000\") and `test_uc_shim_empty_code_follows_occupancy[free]` (line 804, asserts empty for \"\"). In both test_events tests the slot counts as wanted only because a MagicMock coordinator makes `_expects_pin` truthy. Each pins the looping behaviour, so a batch-11 fix or xfail will collide with them."
  },
  {
    "file": "tests/providers/zwave_js/test_e2e.py",
    "line": 1217,
    "summary": "With the `status_only` parametrization removed, the #863 regression test no longer fails when the #863 status-handler guard (`_handle_uc_status_update`'s `_expects_pin` check) is reverted.",
    "failure_scenario": "Replacing `if self._expects_pin(code_slot):` in `_handle_uc_status_update` with `if False:` leaves this test passing: the status event confirms empty and the paired code event overwrites it with known(\"4321\") before any tick. Only older tests catch the mutant: the shared-lock e2e tests (which still feed status-only or code-before-status events the driver never sends) and a test_events unit test. Either keep an e2e detector or treat the guard as dead under the real driver."
  },
  {
    "file": "tests/providers/zwave_js/test_e2e.py",
    "line": 1348,
    "summary": "The settle-before-join uses a bare `async_advance_sync_ticks(hass, freezer, 2)`, which is exactly the minimum: with 1 tick the test fails with 'slot 3 in sync not reached after 8 sync ticks'.",
    "failure_scenario": "Any change to write pacing or to the creating entry's slot count (a third slot in `ZWAVE_JS_LCM_CONFIG_SLOTS`, a longer minimum operation delay) re-opens the overlap. The test then fails as a #1623 regression when the cause is the known open push-cancels-debounced-read bug. Waiting for the creator's slots with `_async_settle_in_sync` on slots 1 and 2 says what is actually needed. No xfail records the open bug either."
  },
  {
    "file": "tests/providers/zwave_js/test_e2e.py",
    "line": 472,
    "summary": "The fake's set always does a verification read-back of the masked code, but the driver's supervised-success path skips that read and persists the cleartext codeData (`#persistCachedUserCode(userId, status, codeData)`); the docstring claims 'A set reads the slot back' with no qualification.",
    "failure_scenario": "A masking lock with Supervision gets cleartext \"9999\" in its value DB and a known(pin) push after the set, not \"****\". The #776 and withheld-code tests cover only the unsupervised path, and the docstring presents the fake as the whole User Code path."
  },
  {
    "file": "tests/providers/zwave_js/test_e2e.py",
    "line": 495,
    "summary": "The fake's clear always sends an Available/\"\" value pair and leaves out the unsupervised clear's verification report. The driver's `#clearCachedUserCodes` only resets values already in the value DB, and the verification GET persists the lock's real report (possibly the leftover or masked code) before the reset.",
    "failure_scenario": "Clearing a slot the value DB has never held makes the fake emit value events (and create values) where the driver emits none. On an unsupervised clear the real sequence is Available plus the lock's leftover, then Available plus \"\", while a pending clear is in flight. The #819 test only sends the leftover later, after settling, so the in-flight ordering is untested."
  },
  {
    "file": "tests/providers/zwave_js/test_e2e.py",
    "line": 367,
    "summary": "`_access_control_event` re-implements the credential-event builders already in `tests/providers/zwave_js/test_events.py` (`_make_credential_added_event` / `_make_credential_modified_event` / deleted).",
    "failure_scenario": "There are now two independent builders for the same driver event payload (`endpointIndex`, `args` keys) in the same provider test package. A schema change in zwave-js-server-python has to be fixed in both, and they can drift silently. Moving one builder into `tests/providers/zwave_js/helpers.py` beside `make_uc_value_event` fixes this."
  },
  {
    "file": "tests/providers/zwave_js/test_e2e.py",
    "line": 1285,
    "summary": "TestMaskingLock's `lock_schlage_be469_state` override deep-copies a dict that the base fixture already loads fresh from JSON for each test (and `lock_schlage_be469` deep-copies again).",
    "failure_scenario": "The copy is redundant: mutating the fixture's own dict in place cannot leak across tests, so the extra `copy` import and deepcopy add nothing."
  }
]
```

